# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF, and Vite's SSR transform mis-handles it: its hashbang
# regex is /^#!.*\n/, and `.` does not match `\r`, so a `#!/usr/bin/env node`
# line ending in CRLF is never detected. Vite then hoists the module's imports
# ABOVE the shebang, producing `...await __vite_ssr_import__(...);#!/usr/bin/env
# node` — a SyntaxError that fails the whole suite at load time. Linux CI never
# saw it because the index is already LF there.
* text=auto eol=lf
